Space exploration drives technological innovation, which often leads to spin-off technologies with commercial applications, boosting the economy.
The global space industry contributes over $400 billion annually to the economy and supports millions of jobs across various sectors.
Investments in space programs have historically led to advancements in fields like telecommunications, GPS, and materials science, creating new industries.
Space-related jobs are high-paying and often require specialized skills, contributing to economic stability and growth.
The development of space infrastructure, such as launch facilities and satellites, stimulates local economies and attracts further investment.